BLIS catalog: third-party files

Each file catalog/models/<name>/config.json is a third-party file: the vendor's model
configuration, copied byte for byte from the repository and revision that the model's
model.yaml names, and redistributed unchanged. It is not licensed under this repository's
Apache-2.0 licence. It remains under the licence that model.yaml's licence.id names.

catalog/licences/index.yaml lists, for every committed config.json whose licence is not
Apache-2.0, the licence, the licence text and any use policy that travel with the file
(in catalog/licences/), the URL each text was read from at a pinned revision, and its
SHA-256. The copyright notices of those files are in those texts.

Some of these licences restrict use. The Llama 2, Llama 3.1, Llama 4, DeepSeek, MiniMax
and Muse Spark Open texts each incorporate a use policy or list of prohibited uses. The
MiniMax-M2.7 licence permits only non-commercial use without MiniMax's prior written
authorisation, and the MiniMax Community Licence (MiniMax-M3) sets conditions on
commercial use. BLIS commits these files for non-commercial research; anyone who uses a
model must read its licence.

The Llama 3.1 and Llama 4 licences (section 1.b.i) ask whoever distributes the materials
to display "Built with Llama", and the Muse Spark Open licence (condition 2) asks a product
that uses the files to display "Built with Muse Spark Open" in its documentation. This
catalog carries those files, and BLIS derives model graphs from them:

